\title{Kneser graph}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2023-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{In 1955 Martin Kneser defined a graph which by now is called the \em{Kneser graph with parameters #{n} and #{k}}. The vertex set of this graph #{KG(n, k)} is #{[n]^{(k)}}, the set of #{k}-subsets of #{[n] = \lbrace 1, \ldots, n\rbrace }, and two #{k}-subsets are adjacent if and only if they are disjoint.}
